{"action":"issue","adjudicationId":"root","baseRevisionId":null,"evidence":[{"digest":"sha256:427537f9898af49bb7e20230201f0ab01db5a51cccbfdb5b57c474e488b3a262","id":"sha256:427537f9898af49bb7e20230201f0ab01db5a51cccbfdb5b57c474e488b3a262","kind":"judgment","relation":"supports"},{"digest":"sha256:575cfe733758035c57b6a7f7915c3e2a38a78c25f4b0c6ce026504546e4655ed","id":"sha256:575cfe733758035c57b6a7f7915c3e2a38a78c25f4b0c6ce026504546e4655ed","kind":"judgment","relation":"supports"},{"digest":"sha256:ae48d86e7bd2cdc4b6c2a708194553c6c8444c7f448bd73a82f8af95b64580c3","id":"sha256:ae48d86e7bd2cdc4b6c2a708194553c6c8444c7f448bd73a82f8af95b64580c3","kind":"judgment","relation":"supports"}],"issuedAtLedgerHead":"b949b704a562aef2692e20ecb661ded7e849f60e","nodeId":"root","nodeType":"root","parentId":null,"reportRef":{"artifact":"report.md","digest":"sha256:ec0c71735572e64c500ce2516aa82d19d6e8b6e1c023b65fb55c81b8ed33b319","section":"## Node: root"},"revisionId":"sha256:3cb47db7505db5566b4294411ed3e7b9a21ddbe0338eec0b3d0bc914c9e028b6","revisionNumber":1,"status":"active","subjects":[],"summary":"The current state records the established equal-area theorem for the four midpoint triangles, its midpoint-segment and altitude-scaling support, and the absence of completed machine-checked formal verification.","title":"Research state for triangle-midpoints"}
{"action":"issue","adjudicationId":"triangle-midpoints/equal-area","baseRevisionId":null,"evidence":[{"digest":"sha256:427537f9898af49bb7e20230201f0ab01db5a51cccbfdb5b57c474e488b3a262","id":"sha256:427537f9898af49bb7e20230201f0ab01db5a51cccbfdb5b57c474e488b3a262","kind":"judgment","relation":"supports"},{"digest":"sha256:575cfe733758035c57b6a7f7915c3e2a38a78c25f4b0c6ce026504546e4655ed","id":"sha256:575cfe733758035c57b6a7f7915c3e2a38a78c25f4b0c6ce026504546e4655ed","kind":"judgment","relation":"supports"},{"digest":"sha256:ae48d86e7bd2cdc4b6c2a708194553c6c8444c7f448bd73a82f8af95b64580c3","id":"sha256:ae48d86e7bd2cdc4b6c2a708194553c6c8444c7f448bd73a82f8af95b64580c3","kind":"judgment","relation":"supports"}],"issuedAtLedgerHead":"b949b704a562aef2692e20ecb661ded7e849f60e","nodeId":"triangle-midpoints/equal-area","nodeType":"claim","parentId":"root","reportRef":{"artifact":"report.md","digest":"sha256:ec0c71735572e64c500ce2516aa82d19d6e8b6e1c023b65fb55c81b8ed33b319","section":"## Node: triangle-midpoints/equal-area"},"revisionId":"sha256:a5d7475675adb2a3dacb5f5f4308b52bca10ef6bff6f727cd9161318d21a6308","revisionNumber":1,"status":"active","subjects":[{"id":"64afc12868e150370e6c56e6eeceab6b7aabe158","kind":"transaction","ledgerPosition":1},{"id":"4ccbe3f18db7402d31a2ef795f6ad67962ff63e3","kind":"transaction","ledgerPosition":2},{"id":"8bcf66bbd7777ee31f637a0a1a144535feb82ba4","kind":"transaction","ledgerPosition":3}],"summary":"For a nondegenerate triangle ABC with side midpoints D, E, and F, the four triangles AEF, BFD, CDE, and DEF each have area one quarter of ABC. The theorem remains valid under the corrected altitude relation and is established as an ordinary mathematical proof, not as a machine-checked formalization.","title":"Equal areas of the four midpoint triangles"}
{"action":"issue","adjudicationId":"triangle-midpoints/midpoint-segment-relations","baseRevisionId":null,"evidence":[{"digest":"sha256:575cfe733758035c57b6a7f7915c3e2a38a78c25f4b0c6ce026504546e4655ed","id":"sha256:575cfe733758035c57b6a7f7915c3e2a38a78c25f4b0c6ce026504546e4655ed","kind":"judgment","relation":"supports"},{"digest":"sha256:427537f9898af49bb7e20230201f0ab01db5a51cccbfdb5b57c474e488b3a262","id":"sha256:427537f9898af49bb7e20230201f0ab01db5a51cccbfdb5b57c474e488b3a262","kind":"judgment","relation":"supports"}],"issuedAtLedgerHead":"b949b704a562aef2692e20ecb661ded7e849f60e","nodeId":"triangle-midpoints/midpoint-segment-relations","nodeType":"lemma","parentId":"triangle-midpoints/equal-area","reportRef":{"artifact":"report.md","digest":"sha256:ec0c71735572e64c500ce2516aa82d19d6e8b6e1c023b65fb55c81b8ed33b319","section":"## Node: triangle-midpoints/midpoint-segment-relations"},"revisionId":"sha256:398ae2cba7cb89dd8cae43376f43c792c6fe9a3e502ff4683608b3bad16577fd","revisionNumber":1,"status":"active","subjects":[{"id":"4ccbe3f18db7402d31a2ef795f6ad67962ff63e3","kind":"transaction","ledgerPosition":2},{"id":"64afc12868e150370e6c56e6eeceab6b7aabe158","kind":"transaction","ledgerPosition":1}],"summary":"The midpoint vector identities imply that EF, FD, and DE are respectively parallel to BC, CA, and AB and have half their corresponding lengths. These relations support half-scale similarity of the medial triangle and the corner-triangle area arguments.","title":"Parallelism and half-length relations for triangle midpoint segments"}
{"action":"issue","adjudicationId":"triangle-midpoints/altitude-scaling","baseRevisionId":null,"evidence":[{"digest":"sha256:ae48d86e7bd2cdc4b6c2a708194553c6c8444c7f448bd73a82f8af95b64580c3","id":"sha256:ae48d86e7bd2cdc4b6c2a708194553c6c8444c7f448bd73a82f8af95b64580c3","kind":"judgment","relation":"supports"}],"issuedAtLedgerHead":"b949b704a562aef2692e20ecb661ded7e849f60e","nodeId":"triangle-midpoints/altitude-scaling","nodeType":"claim","parentId":"triangle-midpoints/equal-area","reportRef":{"artifact":"report.md","digest":"sha256:ec0c71735572e64c500ce2516aa82d19d6e8b6e1c023b65fb55c81b8ed33b319","section":"## Node: triangle-midpoints/altitude-scaling"},"revisionId":"sha256:87a9a2bbb3f5abdd04858323ba2ffecdbea1c75925f1e367248ec1f33bc8b2e3","revisionNumber":1,"status":"active","subjects":[{"id":"8bcf66bbd7777ee31f637a0a1a144535feb82ba4","kind":"transaction","ledgerPosition":3}],"summary":"Under the homothety centered at A with scale factor one half, the distance from A to line EF is half the distance from A to line BC. Parallelism does not make those altitudes equal; scaling both the base and corresponding altitude by one half yields the quarter-area computation. Attribution of the rejected wording to an unavailable external report remains unverified.","title":"Altitude scaling under the midpoint homothety"}
{"action":"issue","adjudicationId":"triangle-midpoints/formal-verification","baseRevisionId":null,"evidence":[{"digest":"sha256:427537f9898af49bb7e20230201f0ab01db5a51cccbfdb5b57c474e488b3a262","id":"sha256:427537f9898af49bb7e20230201f0ab01db5a51cccbfdb5b57c474e488b3a262","kind":"judgment","relation":"qualifies"},{"digest":"sha256:575cfe733758035c57b6a7f7915c3e2a38a78c25f4b0c6ce026504546e4655ed","id":"sha256:575cfe733758035c57b6a7f7915c3e2a38a78c25f4b0c6ce026504546e4655ed","kind":"judgment","relation":"supports"},{"digest":"sha256:ae48d86e7bd2cdc4b6c2a708194553c6c8444c7f448bd73a82f8af95b64580c3","id":"sha256:ae48d86e7bd2cdc4b6c2a708194553c6c8444c7f448bd73a82f8af95b64580c3","kind":"judgment","relation":"supports"}],"issuedAtLedgerHead":"b949b704a562aef2692e20ecb661ded7e849f60e","nodeId":"triangle-midpoints/formal-verification","nodeType":"result","parentId":"triangle-midpoints/equal-area","reportRef":{"artifact":"report.md","digest":"sha256:ec0c71735572e64c500ce2516aa82d19d6e8b6e1c023b65fb55c81b8ed33b319","section":"## Node: triangle-midpoints/formal-verification"},"revisionId":"sha256:6601a38ff97b01f421b89cd70c162499b14d176988f39e2a747722ccee07120b","revisionNumber":1,"status":"active","subjects":[{"id":"64afc12868e150370e6c56e6eeceab6b7aabe158","kind":"transaction","ledgerPosition":1}],"summary":"The evidence establishes an informal Euclidean and vector proof but no completed Lean proof or other machine-checked artifact. Affine-invariance and determinant approaches remain plausible prospective methods, and this verification limitation does not weaken the ordinary proof assessment.","title":"Formal-verification status of the midpoint equal-area theorem"}
